FOURIER TRANSFORMATION TOOLCHAIN
===============================

The toolchain consists of four programs:

  FUNCTION   Generate a table of function values
  GRAPH      Display the table on the R65 display
  TEKGRAPH   Display the table on a Tektronix 4010
  FT         Perform a Fourier transform

Typical workflow:

  FUNCTION TYPE=1 A=1.0 F=10
  GRAPH
  TEKGRAPH
  FT
  GRAPH MODE=ABS

FUNCTION
--------

Generate or modify the current function.

Parameters are entered as

  NAME=value

Several parameters may be entered on one line:

  FUNCTION TYPE=2 A=1.0 B=0.5
  FUNCTION F=25 PHASE=90

If a parameter is omitted, its previous value is
retained.

Available function types:

  1  Cosine
  2  Sum of two cosines
  3  Product of two cosines
  4  Gaussian
  5  Exponential
  6  Rectangular pulse
  7  Trapezoid
  8  Triangle
  9  Sinc

GRAPH
-----

Display the current function table.

GRAPH changes display parameters only. It never
changes the function itself.

Display parameters include

  MODE      REAL IMAG ABS PHASE
  YSCALE    AUTO FULL
  FSCALE    AUTO FULL
  TMIN      Left display limit
  TMAX      Right display limit
  YMIN      Lower Y limit
  YMAX      Upper Y limit

Examples:

  GRAPH
  GRAPH MODE=REAL
  GRAPH MODE=IMAG
  GRAPH YSCALE=FULL

TEKGRAPH
--------

TEKGRAPH has the same parameters as GRAPH but
uses a Tektronix 4010 graphics window.

FT
--

FT transforms the current function table into the
frequency domain.

After FT, GRAPH and TEKGRAPH display the Fourier
transform.

Examples:

  FT
  GRAPH MODE=REAL
  GRAPH MODE=IMAG

Notes
-----

The current function parameters remain unchanged
until another FUNCTION command is issued.

GRAPH and TEKGRAPH only change the display.

A Fourier transform can be repeated after changing
FUNCTION parameters.